  "question": {
    "text": "Let $f(x)=\\int_{\\sin x}^{\\cos x} e^{-t^2} d t$. Then $f^{\\prime}\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{4}\\right)$ equals",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "UT8yE",
      "text": "$\\sqrt{1 / e}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "SVmzF",
      "text": "$-\\sqrt{2 / e}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "0VYUg",
      "text": "$\\sqrt{2 / e}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "E5Foh",
      "text": "$-\\sqrt{1 / e}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$f^{\\prime}(x)=-e^{-\\cos ^2 x} \\sin x-e^{-\\sin ^2 x} \\cos x$\n$\\therefore f^{\\prime}\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{4}\\right)=-e^{-\\frac{1}{2}} \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}-e^{-\\frac{1}{2}} \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}=-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{2 e}}=-\\sqrt{\\frac{2}{e}}$",
    "image": null
  },
